<p>British police are investigating an arson attack in north London after someone set fire to four volunteer ambulances belonging to a Jewish emergency service. The Metropolitan Police are treating the case as a suspected antisemitic hate crime, and counterterrorism officers are leading the inquiry. No injuries were reported in the blaze. Authorities said they are focused on restoring safety and reassuring residents after an attack on emergency vehicles used to help people in need.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/nqt9VAmTcck4cQjLHlkg1-8uAwMNCs0KfSp05ZxcstKdzm5HjCIsI2Acm_oXCfZNOsrM-8O9DlZSP3NiPA2esmMGEUweINxR8wVt0wduDwpbOIL3RxAuA4bU57yaU6RU9Q6P33Rq0-qr3q7KPUNrsTD3ybglURBvGZ6jC32yp7ItQQnJ2LnnStJn4o1Db6vWulvKV7c4O-3wh_yF3zlsb7n7' alt='The scene where police say four ambulances were set on fire in Golders Green.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>At the scene: The ambulances were parked beside a synagogue when firefighters and police arrived in the early hours of Monday.</li><li>Security response: Mark Rowley said police will deploy 264 more officers and highly visible armed patrols to protect Jewish neighborhoods and institutions across London.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Metropolitan Police: The force said it is also examining an online claim of responsibility that appeared after the fire. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/uk-police-probe-attack-jewish-ambulances'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Mark Rowley: The police commissioner pledged 264 extra officers and highly visible armed patrols to help reassure and protect Jewish communities in London. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/uk-police-probe-attack-jewish-ambulances'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/24/g-s1-114920/uk-police-probe-possible-iran-link-after-jewish-charity-ambulances-set-on-fire'>UK police probe possible Iran link after Jewish charity ambulances set on fire</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https